            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0564" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1894</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 29, 5.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. Station agent Vologda received service message that Murman Railroad cut on
                    northern third by Finns. German submarines destroyed Russian wireless station at
                    Murman and sunk Russian freighters, and several Norwegian fish boats in Murman
                    waters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
